Error: Jet.PatternTypeMismatch: Pattern `Box` doesn't say which instance of the generic `Box` it tests
  --> Tests/UI/TraitArmNamesBareGeneric/run.jet:17:9
    |
 17 |         .Box(_) -> 5
    |         ^^^^^^^
 Why: A trait value holds one instance of a generic, and `Box<Int>` and `Box<String>` are different types, so an arm over a trait value spells the instance's type arguments
 Fix: Spell them in the arm, one for each of `Box`'s type parameters (`T`), for example `.Box<Int>(b)`
